Record, Stop, Play, the chevrons and the back arrow are drawn as shapes in
this repository. They are not Iconify icons.

The PC audio link (link/core, and Frame Audio Link in link/addon) codes audio
with Opus. The codec is built in from the unsafe-libopus crate, a Rust
translation of libopus:

- libopus — Copyright 2001-2011 Xiph.Org, Skype Limited, Octasic, Jean-Marc
  Valin, Timothy B. Terriberry, CSIRO, Gregory Maxwell, Mark Borgerding,
  Erik de Castro Lopo. BSD-3-Clause.
  https://opus-codec.org/license/
- unsafe-libopus — DCNick3, BSD-3-Clause
  https://github.com/DCNick3/unsafe-libopus

Frame Audio Link's overlay uses the PC glyph andrsrxn:device-pc-speaker
(Andrés Raxón, MIT), the same one as the mixer panel. It talks to SteamVR
through the OpenVR API (Valve Corporation, BSD-3-Clause), whose library is
loaded from the installed SteamVR and is not shipped. The add-on is built
from Rust crates under MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD and Zlib licenses; `cargo tree`
in link/addon lists them.
